    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"548935\">@Thomas Murrills</span> where does Skimmer stand here?</p>",
        "id": 625581118,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1789931761
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My understanding is that <code>runSkimmer.sh</code> can apply try this: suggestions (and this is already possible for several months). The \"hard part\" here was making deprecations generate these suggestions.</p>",
        "id": 625581173,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1789931803
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Indeed :) It’s exactly the dot notation case that is difficult. (I’ve been focused on getting <code>#find_home</code> over the line + writing some documentation, but hope to return to this soon…though, tooling from the upcoming formatter might be useful in internals here, so it might make sense for certain parts to wait for that in mid-October :) )</p>",
        "id": 625581684,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1789932120
    }
]